WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.203 --> 00:00:03.750
- [Narrator] On September 16th,
22 year old Mahsa Amini died

00:00:03.750 --> 00:00:06.600
after being detained for
allegedly violating Iran's laws

00:00:06.600 --> 00:00:08.640
requiring women to wear a headscarf.

00:00:08.640 --> 00:00:10.530
Iranian authorities say
she died of illness,

00:00:10.530 --> 00:00:12.330
but her family said she fell into a coma

00:00:12.330 --> 00:00:14.790
after being mistreated by police.

00:00:14.790 --> 00:00:17.130
Protests sparked by her death
have since rallied groups

00:00:17.130 --> 00:00:20.580
across Iran's society
from ethnic minorities

00:00:20.580 --> 00:00:24.003
to school children, and even oil workers.

00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:28.320
According to human rights groups,

00:00:28.320 --> 00:00:31.053
clashes with police have
killed more than 200 people.

00:00:32.610 --> 00:00:33.870
But despite the crackdowns

00:00:33.870 --> 00:00:35.520
and widespread internet shutdowns,

00:00:35.520 --> 00:00:37.443
videos have continued to emerge,

00:00:38.310 --> 00:00:40.860
showing how unrest has
spread beyond women's rights

00:00:40.860 --> 00:00:42.900
to a movement that is calling for an end

00:00:42.900 --> 00:00:44.433
to strike theocratic rule.

00:00:45.840 --> 00:00:47.370
These demonstrations have now turned

00:00:47.370 --> 00:00:49.590
into the most broadly
supportive movement in Iran

00:00:49.590 --> 00:00:51.243
in more than four decades.

00:00:54.720 --> 00:00:55.740
A day after her death,

00:00:55.740 --> 00:00:58.563
Amini's funeral took place
in her hometown of Saqqez.

00:00:59.610 --> 00:01:01.710
The ceremony quickly turned into a protest

00:01:01.710 --> 00:01:03.663
against the country's morality police.

00:01:05.010 --> 00:01:06.480
Mourners took off their headscarves

00:01:06.480 --> 00:01:08.250
in defiance of the very rules Amini

00:01:08.250 --> 00:01:10.306
was accused of breaching.

00:01:10.306 --> 00:01:12.390
Amini was Kurdish Iranian,

00:01:12.390 --> 00:01:13.590
part of an ethnic minority

00:01:13.590 --> 00:01:15.030
that has long accused the government

00:01:15.030 --> 00:01:17.250
of discrimination and neglect.

00:01:17.250 --> 00:01:19.860
After a week of unrest,
authorities launched strikes

00:01:19.860 --> 00:01:21.090
at Kurdish militant groups

00:01:21.090 --> 00:01:22.500
across the border in Iraq

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:24.660
saying they were inciting the protests.

00:01:24.660 --> 00:01:26.670
Although there were no
visible separate slogans

00:01:26.670 --> 00:01:29.430
in the protests that
followed Amini's death.

00:01:29.430 --> 00:01:30.360
And the demonstrations

00:01:30.360 --> 00:01:33.573
against Iran's strict Islamic
dress code took on a new form.

00:01:34.500 --> 00:01:36.000
On September 20th, a woman

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:38.640
in the eastern city of
Kerman removed her headscarf

00:01:38.640 --> 00:01:41.583
and cut her hair in a video
that was widely shared online.

00:01:42.570 --> 00:01:44.760
It triggered a wave of
support from around the world

00:01:44.760 --> 00:01:47.100
with celebrities and women
imitating her gesture

00:01:47.100 --> 00:01:49.023
and posting videos to social media.

00:01:51.240 --> 00:01:53.250
That's roughly when the
government restricted access

00:01:53.250 --> 00:01:55.550
to the internet in large
parts of the country.

00:01:56.640 --> 00:01:58.950
Access to platforms like
Instagram and WhatsApp

00:01:58.950 --> 00:02:02.070
that have been used to
organize rallies was blocked.

00:02:02.070 --> 00:02:05.130
The internet cuts through
criticism from businesses.

00:02:05.130 --> 00:02:07.170
Tehran's Chamber of
Commerce estimated the cost

00:02:07.170 --> 00:02:10.683
of $24 billion for industries
including IT services.

00:02:12.480 --> 00:02:13.680
But despite the restrictions,

00:02:13.680 --> 00:02:15.840
the protestors message
was taken up by students

00:02:15.840 --> 00:02:16.983
across the country.

00:02:18.510 --> 00:02:20.498
In one case, children
at an all girls school

00:02:20.498 --> 00:02:22.920
took off their scarves
and chased away a man

00:02:22.920 --> 00:02:24.030
from the premises,

00:02:24.030 --> 00:02:26.283
throwing bottles and chanting shameless.

00:02:29.580 --> 00:02:31.800
As more crowds took to the
streets in large numbers,

00:02:31.800 --> 00:02:34.140
the government used tear
gas and live ammunition

00:02:34.140 --> 00:02:35.883
to disperse demonstrations.

00:02:37.200 --> 00:02:39.960
A particularly deadly incident
broke down the southeast,

00:02:39.960 --> 00:02:42.273
home to another ethnic
minority, the Baluch.

00:02:43.440 --> 00:02:45.480
On September 30th, protestors were seen

00:02:45.480 --> 00:02:49.080
walking towards a police
station before being fired upon.

00:02:49.080 --> 00:02:51.660
Local human rights groups
say more than 90 people

00:02:51.660 --> 00:02:55.020
were killed in what protestors
dubbed "bloody Friday."

00:02:55.020 --> 00:02:57.510
The government blamed the
violence on a local militant group

00:02:57.510 --> 00:02:59.703
that has denied any role in the protests.

00:03:01.380 --> 00:03:02.820
And then demonstrations spread

00:03:02.820 --> 00:03:05.913
to one of the most critical
sectors of Iran's economy, oil.

00:03:06.960 --> 00:03:08.850
In early October, workers went on strike

00:03:08.850 --> 00:03:11.760
at a number of refineries,
blocking roads with stones

00:03:11.760 --> 00:03:14.670
and chanting slogans in
support of other protests.

00:03:14.670 --> 00:03:16.500
Although the government
claimed these strikes

00:03:16.500 --> 00:03:18.870
weren't related to Amini's death.

00:03:18.870 --> 00:03:20.700
These strikes highlight
another big problem

00:03:20.700 --> 00:03:22.260
for the Islamic republic,

00:03:22.260 --> 00:03:24.417
a struggling economy due to US sanctions

00:03:24.417 --> 00:03:27.180
and a number of other
issues in the country

00:03:27.180 --> 00:03:29.520
and they have a symbolic weight in Iran.

00:03:29.520 --> 00:03:32.430
It was strikes to oil refineries in 1978,

00:03:32.430 --> 00:03:34.110
much bigger ones than today

00:03:34.110 --> 00:03:35.820
that helped bring down the Shah of Iran,

00:03:35.820 --> 00:03:37.380
Mohammad Reza Pahlavi,

00:03:37.380 --> 00:03:38.970
in the revolution that established

00:03:38.970 --> 00:03:40.533
the current Islamic republic.

00:03:41.640 --> 00:03:43.140
In recent years Iran's leaders

00:03:43.140 --> 00:03:44.850
have faced several protest movements,

00:03:44.850 --> 00:03:46.740
but have shown no sign of backing down

00:03:46.740 --> 00:03:48.600
and today is no different.

00:03:48.600 --> 00:03:50.610
They claim the demonstrations
are being orchestrated

00:03:50.610 --> 00:03:51.780
by foreign enemies,

00:03:51.780 --> 00:03:55.260
and hundreds of protestors
have been brought to trial.

00:03:55.260 --> 00:03:57.000
But discontent has continued to emerge

00:03:57.000 --> 00:03:59.670
across society disrupting normal life.

00:03:59.670 --> 00:04:01.590
From this prison that was engulfed by fire

00:04:01.590 --> 00:04:05.160
after a clash between
detainees and prison guards

00:04:05.160 --> 00:04:07.860
to shopkeepers striking across the country

00:04:07.860 --> 00:04:09.720
and a major target of the demonstrations

00:04:09.720 --> 00:04:11.520
continues to be one of the foundations

00:04:11.520 --> 00:04:12.990
of the theocratic state.

00:04:12.990 --> 00:04:15.219
Its Supreme leader, Ali Khamenei.

00:04:15.219 --> 00:04:17.969
(crowd chanting)

